  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Introduction</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Sports Bra Manufacturer for Performance Activewear Brands</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>As a specialized sports bra manufacturer based in Bangladesh, SDF Clothing understands that support, comfort, and durability are non-negotiable requirements for activewear brands. The sports bra market demands precise engineering to provide appropriate support levels for different activities while maintaining comfort during extended wear. Our facility delivers on these requirements with minimum orders of 300 pieces, making professional manufacturing accessible to emerging fitness brands and established labels expanding their activewear collections.</p>
        
        <p>Bangladesh has developed particular expertise in activewear manufacturing, with specialized factories focused on performance fabrics and technical construction methods. Our sports bra production leverages this expertise, offering international brands access to skilled labor, competitive pricing, and established supply chains for performance materials. The 300-piece minimum enables brands to test different support levels and styles without committing to large inventory positions, reducing risk while accessing factory-direct pricing.</p>
        
        <p>Our sports bra manufacturing addresses the technical challenges that distinguish quality sports bras from standard lingerie: appropriate support levels for different activities, moisture management for comfort during exercise, secure construction that withstands repeated washing and high-impact movement, and design features that balance functionality with aesthetic appeal. We work with nylon-spandex, polyester-spandex, and recycled fabric blends to achieve these performance characteristics while offering options for sustainable materials.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Product Range</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">What We Manufacture</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Our sports bra production encompasses multiple support levels and design configurations designed for different activities and body types. Each style maintains our commitment to performance fabrics and quality construction while offering distinct functional characteristics. We manufacture all styles from 300 pieces minimum, with the ability to mix support levels and designs within larger orders for comprehensive collections.</p>
        
        <p>Low impact sports bras are designed for yoga, pilates, walking, and stretching activities where breast movement is minimal. These styles prioritize comfort and freedom of movement over maximum support. Low impact bras typically feature lighter-weight fabrics in the 200-220 GSM range, wider straps for comfort without pressure points, and simpler construction methods that emphasize natural shape. The band construction provides gentle support without compression that might restrict breathing during gentle activities. Low impact styles are ideal for wellness-focused brands and customers prioritizing comfort over high-performance support.</p>
        
        <p>Medium impact sports bras serve the needs of cyclists, hikers, strength trainers, and participants in moderate-intensity fitness classes. These styles require more substantial construction than low impact options, typically using fabrics in the 220-250 GSM range with increased compression. Medium impact bras feature wider bands for stability, reinforced stitching at stress points, and strategic panel placement to control movement. Strap configurations may include racerback designs for added stability or traditional straps for versatility. This support level represents the largest segment of the sports bra market, serving customers who engage in regular fitness activities without requiring maximum support.</p>
        
        <p>High impact sports bras are engineered for running, HIIT workouts, team sports, and other activities with significant vertical movement. These styles demand the most robust construction, using fabrics in the 250-280 GSM range with maximum compression and recovery properties. High impact bras feature wide, reinforced bands often with double-layer construction, encapsulation design that separates and supports each breast, and multiple strap configurations including cross-back and racerback designs that distribute pressure evenly. The construction methods used in high impact bras are similar to those used in compression garments, with careful attention to seam placement to prevent chafing during intense activity.</p>
        
        <p>Racerback sports bras feature straps that meet between the shoulder blades, providing added stability and preventing strap slippage during movement. This configuration is particularly popular for running and high-intensity activities where shoulder stability is important. Racerback designs can be produced in all support levels, with construction adjustments to ensure the strap junction provides adequate support without creating pressure points. The racerback configuration also offers aesthetic appeal, with many customers preferring the athletic appearance and freedom of arm movement this design provides.</p>
        
        <p>Strappy back sports bras incorporate decorative strap configurations on the back panel, creating visual interest while maintaining functional support. These designs require sophisticated pattern engineering to ensure that decorative straps do not compromise structural integrity. Our strappy designs use reinforced base layers with overlay straps that provide aesthetic detail without bearing the primary support load. Strappy back styles typically have a 500-piece minimum due to increased production complexity and are popular in fashion-forward activewear markets where aesthetics are as important as functionality.</p>
        
        <p>Underwire sports bras provide enhanced support and shaping for customers who prefer the structure and lift that underwire provides. Underwire sports bras require specialized construction to ensure the wire channel is properly encased and positioned to prevent discomfort during movement. The wire must be flexible enough to move with the body while maintaining shape, and the surrounding construction must distribute pressure evenly. Underwire styles are typically positioned as premium options within sports bra collections and require careful fit testing to ensure comfort during activity.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-wrapper">
        <table class="comparison">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Support Level</th>
              <th>Best For</th>
              <th>Fabric GSM</th>
              <th>Key Features</th>
              <th>Price Tier</th>
            </tr>
