  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Production Process</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Our Manufacturing Process</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Our sports bra manufacturing follows a precision process designed to ensure consistent support, fit, and quality across production runs. The process typically spans 60-75 days for first-time orders including sampling and production, with 45-60 days for repeat orders using approved fabrics and patterns. Sports bras require particular attention to fit testing and support verification, which extends the sampling phase compared to simpler garments.</p>
        
        <p>The process begins with technical specification review, where we analyze your requirements including target support level, cup preferences, size chart, fabric requirements, and performance testing criteria. Sports bras require more detailed specifications than basic garments, including measurements for band tension, strap width, and cup depth. Our team provides feedback on technical feasibility and may suggest modifications to optimize manufacturability while maintaining design intent. This stage takes 2-3 days and ensures technical alignment before sampling begins.</p>
        
        <p>Fabric sourcing and testing follows specification review, taking 10-15 days for standard fabrics and 15-20 days for custom fabric development. Sports bra fabrics undergo rigorous testing for stretch recovery, compression properties, and durability before approval. We test fabrics for elongation and recovery to ensure they maintain shape through repeated wear, wash testing to verify durability, and color fastness testing to ensure colors remain vibrant. If you require custom fabric development for specific colors or performance properties, we coordinate with mills to produce sample yardage for testing.</p>
        
        <p>Sample development for sports bras takes 15-20 days, longer than basic garments due to the need for fit testing and support verification. Initial samples focus on construction and basic fit, with subsequent samples refining strap placement, band tension, and cup configuration. We provide detailed measurement reports and conduct fit tests on multiple size points to verify consistent support across the size range. Sports bra samples require wear testing to verify support levels during actual activity, which may extend the sampling timeline if multiple iterations are needed.</p>
        
        <p>Support level verification is a critical step in sports bra sampling that we conduct in partnership with your team. We test low, medium, and high impact designs to verify they provide appropriate support for their intended activities. This testing may include subjective fit assessments by wear testers and objective measurements of breast displacement during movement. Support verification ensures that the final product meets performance expectations and reduces the risk of returns due to inadequate support.</p>
        
        <p>Pattern grading for sports bras requires specialized expertise to ensure consistent support across sizes. The relationship between band size and cup size must be carefully maintained through grading to ensure that a 34C provides the same relative support as a 38C. Our pattern makers use graded measurement systems that account for this relationship, producing size sets from XS to 4XL that maintain proportional support. Grading takes 3-5 days and includes verification of strap width scaling, band tension consistency, and cup volume proportionality.</p>
        
        <p>Bulk production for sports bras spans 30-40 days from fabric receipt, with complex designs such as strappy backs requiring 35-45 days. Cutting is performed with attention to grain line orientation to ensure consistent stretch properties. Sewing lines are staffed by operators trained in activewear construction, with particular expertise in elastic application, strap construction, and cup insertion. Quality checkpoints at each sewing operation verify seam integrity, elastic tension, and component placement. Throughout production, we conduct in-line testing of band tension and strap security to catch issues early.</p>
        
        <p>Final quality inspection uses AQL 2.5 standards for major defects and AQL 4.0 for minor defects, with additional testing for sports bra-specific criteria. Inspection includes band tension testing using calibrated tension meters, strap pull testing to verify attachment strength, and cup placement verification. We also conduct random wash testing on production samples to verify that garments maintain their support properties after laundering. Detailed inspection reports with photos are provided before shipment, and any defects found are rectified before goods leave our facility.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Materials</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Fabric & Material Options</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Fabric selection is critical to sports bra performance, affecting support, comfort, moisture management, and durability. We offer multiple fabric options optimized for different support levels and performance requirements. All fabrics are tested for stretch recovery, compression properties, and durability to ensure they meet the demands of athletic wear.</p>
        
        <p>Nylon-spandex blends, typically in 80/20 or 82/18 ratios, are the premium choice for sports bra construction. Nylon provides excellent durability, abrasion resistance, and a smooth hand feel against the skin, while spandex delivers the stretch and recovery essential for support garments. Nylon-spandex fabrics offer superior moisture-wicking compared to other blends, moving perspiration away from the skin during intense activity. These fabrics typically range from 200-280 GSM, with higher GSM providing more compression for high-impact support. Nylon-spandex is our recommendation for premium positioning and high-performance sports bras.</p>
        
        <p>Polyester-spandex blends, usually 85/15 or 88/12, offer cost efficiency with good performance characteristics. Polyester provides excellent color retention and durability, making it suitable for sports bras in bold colors that require repeated washing. The fiber's inherent resistance to pilling maintains appearance through extended wear. Polyester-spandex fabrics range from 200-260 GSM and are ideal for value-positioned lines or fashion-focused sports bras where performance requirements are moderate. Performance finishes can enhance moisture management on polyester bases to approach nylon performance.</p>
        
        <p>Recycled polyester-spandex fabrics, certified by GRS (Global Recycled Standard), provide sustainable options without compromising performance. These fabrics are made from post-consumer plastic bottles, processed into polyester fiber and blended with spandex for stretch. Recycled fabrics offer the same durability, color retention, and performance as virgin polyester, with the added benefit of environmental certification. GRS certification requires traceability throughout the supply chain, providing documentation for sustainability marketing. Recycled fabrics typically cost 10-15% more than conventional polyester but appeal to eco-conscious consumers.</p>
        
        <p>Moisture-wicking mesh panels are incorporated into sports bra designs to enhance ventilation in high-sweat areas. These mesh fabrics feature open constructions that promote airflow while maintaining structural integrity. Mesh is typically used in back panels, center front inserts, or as strategic ventilation zones. The mesh must be carefully integrated with supportive base fabrics to ensure that ventilation does not compromise support. We offer mesh in matching colors to main fabrics or in contrasting colors for design accent.</p>
        
        <p>Power mesh lining is used in high-impact sports bras to provide additional support and compression. This fine-gauge mesh has high compression properties and is often used as a second layer in encapsulation designs or as lining in compression bands. Power mesh maintains breathability while adding structural support, making it ideal for running bras and other high-impact applications. The mesh is applied with careful attention to seam placement to prevent irritation against the skin.</p>
        
        <p>Cup materials include standard foam pads in varying thicknesses, molded cups for enhanced shaping, and fiberfill options for natural feel. Foam cups provide lightweight padding and modesty without adding significant bulk, available in thicknesses from 3mm to 10mm depending on desired coverage. Molded cups offer pre-formed shapes that provide consistent appearance and enhanced shaping, particularly popular in medium-impact styles. Fiberfill cups provide natural feel and breathability, ideal for low-impact styles where comfort is prioritized over shaping. All cup materials are encased in fabric pockets that allow removal for washing and replacement.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-wrapper">
        <table class="comparison">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Material</th>
              <th>Composition</th>
              <th>GSM Range</th>
              <th>Key Properties</th>
              <th>Best For</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Nylon-Spandex</td>
              <td>80/20 or 82/18</td>
              <td>200-280</td>
              <td>Premium stretch, moisture-wicking, durable</td>
              <td>High impact, premium positioning</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Polyester-Spandex</td>
              <td>85/15 or 88/12</td>
              <td>200-260</td>
              <td>Color-fast, cost-efficient, pill-resistant</td>
              <td>Value positioning, fashion styles</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Recycled Polyester-Spandex</td>
              <td>85/15 (GRS certified)</td>
              <td>200-260</td>
              <td>Sustainable, durable, certified</td>
              <td>Eco-conscious brands, sustainability</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Moisture-Wicking Mesh</td>
              <td>Nylon or polyester blend</td>
              <td>150-180</td>
              <td>Ventilation, breathable, lightweight</td>
              <td>Ventilation panels, back designs</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Power Mesh Lining</td>
              <td>Nylon-spandex</td>
              <td>180-220</td>
              <td>High compression, supportive, breathable</td>
              <td>High impact, encapsulation</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
          <caption>All fabrics tested for stretch recovery and compression properties. Custom GSM available.</caption>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Bangladesh Advantage</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Why Source Sports Bras from Bangladesh</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Bangladesh has emerged as a competitive sourcing destination for sports bras and activewear, combining cost advantages with developing technical expertise. The country's garment industry has evolved beyond basic cut-and-sew operations to include sophisticated activewear production capable of meeting the technical requirements of performance sports bras. This evolution, combined with competitive labor costs and established infrastructure, makes Bangladesh an attractive option for sports bra manufacturing.</p>
        
        <p>Labor costs in Bangladesh are significantly lower than in China, Vietnam, or Turkey, translating to 15-25% cost savings on finished sports bras. However, the cost advantage does not come at the expense of quality. The Bangladeshi garment industry has invested in specialized training for activewear production, with operators developing expertise in elastic application, stretch fabric handling, and the precise construction methods required for supportive sports bras. Our facility conducts regular training programs to ensure operators are proficient in the latest sports bra construction techniques.</p>
        
        <p>Bangladesh's domestic fabric supply includes mills capable of producing nylon-spandex and polyester-spandex blends suitable for sports bra construction. While specialized performance fabrics with proprietary finishes may still require import, the base fabric supply is well-established locally. This local sourcing reduces lead times and logistics costs compared to countries that rely entirely on imported fabrics. Our relationships with local fabric mills ensure priority allocation and consistent quality for sports bra fabrics.</p>
        
        <p>The country's export infrastructure includes experienced freight forwarders, customs brokers, and documentation specialists familiar with garment export requirements. Shipments from Bangladesh to major markets are routine, with multiple weekly sailings to Europe and North America. Air freight options are available for urgent orders, though ocean freight is more cost-effective for standard production volumes. The established export infrastructure reduces the risk of delays and documentation errors that can occur with less experienced sourcing locations.</p>
        
        <p>Following the comprehensive reforms after 2013, workplace safety and social compliance in Bangladesh's garment industry have come a long way. Our facility holds BSCI certification, which covers fair wages, reasonable working hours, and safe working conditions, giving activewear and sports bra brands a documented basis for the ethical sourcing claims they make to their own customers. Retailers now weigh this heavily, and it substantially cuts the reputational risk that used to be attached to Bangladesh sourcing.</p>
        
        <p>Duty-free access to European markets through the Everything But Arms (EBA) arrangement provides Bangladesh garments with preferential tariff treatment, reducing import costs for EU customers. Similar preferential access exists for other markets including Canada, Australia, and Japan. This duty advantage can significantly impact landed costs, making Bangladesh-sourced sports bras more competitive in these markets. For brands targeting EU distribution, the duty savings can offset other costs and improve overall margins.</p>
        
        <p>The Bangladesh garment industry has developed specialized expertise in stretch garment production, which directly translates to sports bra manufacturing. Handling stretch fabrics, applying elastic with consistent tension, and constructing garments that maintain shape through wear are well-established skills in the country's workforce. This specialized expertise reduces the learning curve for new sports bra styles and ensures consistent quality across production runs. The industry's experience with international brands also means that quality expectations and communication standards are well-understood.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">International Shipping</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Shipping to UK, USA, Australia & EU</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>We ship sports bras to major international markets including the United Kingdom, United States, Australia, and European Union countries. Each market has specific requirements for documentation, duties, and shipping timelines that we navigate routinely. Our experience with international sports bra shipments ensures your goods arrive on time and with proper documentation for customs clearance.</p>
        
        <p>Shipments to the United Kingdom typically take 30-35 days by ocean freight, including transit time and customs clearance. Air freight options reduce this to 7-10 days at significantly higher cost. The UK applies import duties on garments from Bangladesh, though rates vary by fabric composition and declared value. Sports bras typically fall under specific HS codes that may have different duty rates than other garments. We provide accurate classification and valuation to ensure proper duty calculation. Post-Brexit documentation requirements are handled to ensure smooth customs clearance.</p>
        
        <p>United States shipments take 25-30 days by ocean freight to West Coast ports and 35-40 days to East Coast ports. Air freight takes 5-7 days to major US airports. The US maintains normal trade relations with Bangladesh, with standard MFN duty rates applying to sports bras. The US has specific labeling requirements for garments including fiber content in English and country of origin. We ensure all labels meet US Federal Trade Commission requirements. US customs may also inspect for compliance with textile fiber identification rules, which we address through proper documentation.</p>
        
        <p>Australia shipments take 20-25 days by ocean freight to major ports including Sydney, Melbourne, and Brisbane. Air freight takes 7-10 days. Australia maintains a free trade agreement with Bangladesh that eliminates duties on many garments, though specific rules of origin must be met. We ensure our production processes meet these origin requirements to qualify for duty-free entry. Australia's strict biosecurity requirements are addressed through proper packaging and documentation to prevent clearance delays.</p>
        
        <p>European Union shipments benefit from duty-free access under the Everything But Arms arrangement for least-developed countries. Ocean freight takes 28-32 days to Northern European ports and 32-38 days to Southern European ports. Air freight takes 5-8 days. EU countries require specific documentation including certificates of origin, commercial invoices with detailed descriptions, and conformity declarations for certain materials. The EU also has specific requirements for textile labeling including fiber content percentages and care instructions in the language of the destination country.</p>
        
        <p>Documentation for all markets includes commercial invoices, packing lists, bills of lading, certificates of origin, and any required certificates for regulated materials. For sports bras, this may include certificates for fabric content and any performance claims. We provide all documentation in English and can arrange for translations if required by specific markets. Our documentation is prepared to meet both customs requirements and your internal accounting needs, with clear descriptions and accurate valuations.</p>
        
        <p>Incoterms can be structured according to your preferences, including FOB (Free On Board) Bangladesh for maximum control, CIF (Cost, Insurance, Freight) to destination port for convenience, or DDP (Delivered Duty Paid) for complete door-to-door service. We recommend FOB for experienced importers with established freight forwarding relationships, as this typically provides the best overall cost. CIF and DDP options are available for brands seeking simplified logistics or those new to international sourcing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Certifications</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Quality Standards & Certifications</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Quality assurance and certification are fundamental to our sports bra manufacturing process. Sports bras require particular attention to quality control due to their functional nature and the physical demands placed on them during activity. We maintain multiple certifications that verify our commitment to quality, social responsibility, and environmental standards.</p>
        
        <p>OEKO-TEX Standard 100 certification applies to our fabrics, ensuring they are free from harmful substances including heavy metals, pesticides, and formaldehyde. This certification is particularly important for sports bras that have prolonged skin contact during exercise and perspiration. OEKO-TEX testing covers all fabric components including base materials, elastics, trims, and cup materials. We provide OEKO-TEX certificates for each material lot, enabling you to substantiate claims about chemical safety in your marketing materials.</p>
        
        <p>GRS (Global Recycled Standard) certification applies to our recycled polyester fabrics, verifying the recycled content and ensuring traceability throughout the supply chain. GRS certification covers environmental and social criteria for recycled material production, including wastewater treatment, chemical restrictions, and labor practices. If you choose recycled fabrics for your sports bras, GRS certification provides credible substantiation for sustainability claims and is increasingly required by major retailers for recycled content products.</p>
        
        <p>We hold BSCI (Business Social Compliance Initiative) certification, verified by independent third-party auditors against fair wages, reasonable working hours, prohibition of child labor, and safe working conditions. For sports bra and activewear brands whose customers already tend to ask harder questions about supply chains, having that third-party verification on file makes it easier to demonstrate supply chain responsibility rather than just asserting it.</p>
        
        <p>ISO 9001 certification applies to our quality management system, ensuring consistent processes for production and quality control. ISO 9001 requires documented procedures for all critical processes, regular internal audits, and continuous improvement. This certification provides assurance that our quality systems are systematic and repeatable, reducing variability between production runs. For sports bras, this means consistent support, fit, and construction across orders, which is critical for customer satisfaction and return reduction.</p>
        
        <p>WRAP (Worldwide Responsible Accredited Production) certification is another social compliance certification we maintain, focusing specifically on workplace conditions and worker rights. WRAP certification covers similar ground to BSCI but with different audit methodology and emphasis. Holding multiple social compliance certifications provides flexibility to meet various retailer requirements, as different buyers may specify different certification preferences in their vendor codes of conduct.</p>
        
        <p>Internal quality control processes supplement these certifications with day-to-day assurance specific to sports bra production. We conduct in-line inspections during production, testing band tension at regular intervals, verifying strap attachment strength, and checking cup placement accuracy. Final inspection includes functional testing beyond visual inspection, including tension testing and wash testing on random samples. We maintain records of all testing results, enabling traceability if issues arise after delivery. These internal processes ensure certifications translate to actual quality in finished sports bras.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Getting Started</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">How to Get Started</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Starting your sports bra production with SDF Clothing follows a structured process designed to ensure your support requirements are met and quality expectations are understood from the outset. The process begins with providing detailed specifications, after which we guide you through sampling, support verification, and production. Understanding these steps upfront helps you prepare the information we need for accurate quoting and efficient production.</p>
        
        <p>Step one is to submit your technical specifications through our contact form or email. Sports bras require more detailed specifications than basic garments. Essential information includes: target support level (low, medium, or high impact), cup preferences (unlined, removable cups, or molded), size chart or target market sizing, band width preferences, strap configuration (traditional, racerback, or strappy), fabric preferences or performance requirements, target quantity per style and color, and desired delivery timeline. If you have technical drawings, photos of reference samples, or existing products you want to replicate, include these for clarity.</p>
        
        <p>Step two involves our technical review and quotation process. Within 24-48 hours of receiving your specifications, we provide a detailed quotation including fabric costs, production costs, sampling costs, and estimated shipping costs. The quotation specifies lead times for sampling and production, minimum order quantities, and payment terms. For sports bras, we may ask clarifying questions about support requirements or suggest modifications to optimize manufacturability while maintaining your design intent. You may request revisions to the quotation to adjust specifications to meet budget targets.</p>
        
        <p>Step three is sample development and support verification. After quotation acceptance, we proceed with sample development, typically taking 15-20 days. Samples are shipped to you for review, and we provide detailed measurement reports. For sports bras, we recommend wear testing samples to verify support levels for intended activities. You may approve samples as-is, request modifications to support or fit, or proceed with additional sample rounds. Each sample round adds 7-10 days but ensures the final product meets performance expectations. We recommend thorough testing including wash testing and activity-specific wear testing before approval.</p>
        
        <p>Step four is production confirmation. Once samples are approved and support levels are verified, we require a deposit to confirm production and initiate fabric procurement. Standard terms are 30% deposit with order confirmation and 70% before shipment. Production begins after deposit receipt and fabric availability is confirmed. We provide a production schedule with key milestones including cutting completion, sewing completion, and expected shipment date. Throughout production, we provide status updates and may send photos of goods in process for your review.</p>
        
        <p>Step five is final inspection and shipment. Before shipment, we conduct final quality inspection using AQL standards with additional testing for sports bra-specific criteria including band tension and strap strength. We provide an inspection report for your review. Once inspection is approved, we finalize packaging and prepare shipping documentation. Balance payment is required before release of shipping documents. We provide all necessary documentation including commercial invoice, packing list, bill of lading, certificates of origin, and any required certificates for regulated materials. Goods are released to your nominated freight forwarder or ours depending on agreed Incoterms.</p>
        
        <p>Throughout the process, our team provides technical guidance on sports bra construction, support level selection, and fabric choices. We understand that sports bras are technical products with specific performance requirements, and we work to ensure these requirements are met through manufacturing expertise rather than relying solely on trial and error. Clear communication about support expectations and activity targets helps us deliver products that perform as intended.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
