        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Sports Bra Manufacturer FAQ</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq">
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What is the minimum order quantity for sports bras?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Our minimum order quantity for custom sports bras is 300 pieces per style. This minimum allows you to access factory-direct pricing while testing market response with manageable inventory. The 300-piece minimum can be distributed across sizes within a single colorway. Lower quantities are available for sampling and prototype development at higher per-piece costs for brands requiring smaller initial runs or needing to test multiple styles before committing to bulk production.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What support levels do you offer for sports bras?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">We manufacture sports bras in three support levels: low impact for yoga, pilates, and walking; medium impact for cycling, hiking, and strength training; and high impact for running, HIIT, and team sports. Support level is determined through fabric selection, construction methods, and design features such as band width and strap configuration. We can help you select the appropriate support level for your target market and intended activities based on our experience with various fitness segments.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">Do you offer sports bras with removable cups?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Yes. Removable cup options are available across all support levels. We offer standard foam cups in varying thicknesses from 3mm to 10mm, molded cups for enhanced shaping, and fiberfill options for natural feel. Cup pockets are constructed with secure closures to prevent shifting during activity. Removable cups add approximately $0.50-1.00 per piece depending on cup type and can be omitted for customers who prefer unpadded styles or for low-impact designs where modesty is less of a concern.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What fabric options are available for sports bras?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">We offer nylon-spandex blends (80/20 or 82/18) for premium performance with superior stretch and recovery, polyester-spandex blends for durability and color retention, recycled polyester-spandex certified by GRS for sustainable options, and moisture-wicking mesh panels for ventilation. Fabric GSM ranges from 200-280 depending on support requirements, with higher GSM providing more compression and support for high-impact activities. All fabrics are tested for stretch recovery and compression properties before use.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">Can you produce strappy and fashion-forward sports bra designs?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Yes. We produce strappy back designs, racerback configurations, cross-back straps, keyhole cutouts, and other fashion-forward details. Complex strap designs require specialized construction techniques to maintain support while achieving aesthetic goals. Our pattern makers ensure that decorative elements do not compromise structural integrity. Fashion styles typically have a 500-piece minimum due to increased production complexity compared to standard designs. We can provide guidance on which decorative features are compatible with different support levels.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">How long does sports bra production take?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Standard production timeline is 30-40 days from fabric receipt for basic sports bras. Custom fabric development adds 15-20 days. Sampling takes 15-20 days before bulk production approval. Complex designs with strappy details or custom molding may require 35-45 days production time. We recommend planning 60-75 days total from initial inquiry to delivery for first-time orders including sampling and production, or 45-60 days for repeat orders using approved materials and patterns.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
